@@ -19,6 +19,50 @@ Set `PORT` to choose a different port and `DATA_DIR` to choose a data folder. Th
 
 The provider is deterministic and supports the documented prompt patterns. Other prompts receive its general echo response. See [the provider guide](provider/README.md) and [the records guide](records/README.md) for examples and permissions.
 
+## What to expect
+
+**Bots, conversations and saved items**
+
+- Bot names can repeat; each one is a separate bot. Messages show the bot's current name, so renaming a bot also relabels its earlier messages.
+- A conversation's title is the first message sent in it, with spaces and line breaks collapsed, cut to 56 characters. When two of the open bot's conversations have the same title, the list also shows the latest message you sent in each. New bots and conversations are listed first.
+- Saved instructions and saved tasks belong to the person and are shared by all of that person's bots. Each bot uses at most one instruction at a time. Editing or deleting an instruction changes every bot that uses it.
+- Saving an instruction or task under a name that is already saved is refused with an alert, and the saved one is unchanged. Choose **Edit <name>** to change it, or pick another name.
+- Limits: bot, instruction and task names 80 characters; instruction text and task requests 6,000; messages and memory text 12,000. A field over its limit says how much to remove and cannot be sent or saved until it is shortened. Nothing is cut off.
+
+**Your place in a conversation**
+
+- The starter examples put a prompt in the composer for you to review and send. They ask before replacing a message you have not sent.
+- Unsent drafts and your reading position in each conversation are kept in this browser's storage, per person, so a reload or a later visit opens the same place. **Switch person** clears them from this browser.
+- A failed reply keeps its alert and **Retry** under its message, even after you send later messages. The retried reply appears directly after the message it answers.
+
+**Memory**
+
+- Remembering and forgetting treat facts that differ only in capitals as the same fact. Forgetting removes the memory entry; the conversation where it was said is unchanged.
+
+**Records and proposals**
+
+- Only these fields of existing records can change: an order's `customer`, `status` and `total`, and an account's `name`, `tier` and `owner`. A new value keeps the field's type (a number for `total`).
+- The provider matches field names exactly as written, so write them in lowercase. `What is the STATUS of ORD-1001?` gets "ORD-1001 has no STATUS.", and `set the Status of ORD-1001 to closed` is refused with a **Change result** that lists the fields you can change.
+- `create an order for <customer> totalling <number>` takes whole numbers only. With a decimal such as `35.50` the provider gives its echo reply and no proposal. `set the total of ORD-1001 to 35.50` works and shows `35.5`.
+- Amounts larger than 9007199254740991 cannot be kept exactly, so they are refused before **Confirm changes** is offered.
+- A pending creation reserves the order ID it shows, across people and conversations. Rejecting it frees that ID for the next preview; other open previews keep the IDs they show.
+- **Confirm changes** checks that each field still has the value you reviewed. If a field was changed and then changed back to that value, the earlier proposal still applies.
+
+**Long tasks**
+
+- `add step: ...` adds to the task running in the same conversation. When more than one is running, the app asks which one gets the step (**Add to <task>** or **Don’t add**). A note under the reply says where the step went, or that it was not added.
+- If progress cannot be saved, for example because the data folder became unavailable, the task turns **Interrupted** once saving works again, and **Retry task** continues from the last finished step. Node logs the task and the error.
+- **Since you were away** lists running tasks, tasks that need attention, and tasks that finished while you were away (since this browser last closed or hid the page), apart from those that finished during this visit. In a browser that has not opened the app before, every finished task counts as finished while away. Selecting a task opens its conversation and moves to the task.
+
+**What the stand-in provider answers**
+
+- Questions outside the provider guide's patterns, such as "Which of my open orders has the biggest total?", get its echo reply ("You said: ..."), not an answer.
+- A finished research task lists one acknowledgment per step, such as `Done: Write the summary of monthly order review`. The provider does not return findings or a written summary.
+
+**The provider token**
+
+- A valid `PROVIDER_TOKEN` takes precedence over a saved token; an invalid one is ignored and the saved token is used. A token saved through **Setup** is stored as plain text in `workspace.json` under `DATA_DIR`, a file only the account running Node can read. The app never shows it in a page or response.
+
 ## Verify
 
 Run `npm test` for the native Node suite. The optional browser check, `node test/browser.cjs`, needs Chrome. Set `CHROME_BIN` if Chrome is installed at a nonstandard path.
